//!
//! # Lib
//!
//! Small building blocks that depend on nothing else in the kernel: memory
//! primitives, integer formatting and the keyboard scancode ring buffer.
//!
//! ## Public API
//!
//! | Namespace            | File                | Purpose                                           |
//! |----------------------|---------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Lib::Mem`           | `mem.ign`           | `memcpy`, `memset`, `memmove`, `memcmp`           |
//! | `Lib::Format`        | `format.ign`        | decimal and hexadecimal text through a callback   |
//! | `Lib::ScancodeQueue` | `scancode_queue.ign`| lock-free ring buffer between IRQ1 and the shell  |
//!
//! ## Dependencies
//!
//! None. Every other subsystem may import `Lib`:
//!
//! ```ignis
//! import Lib from "@lib";
//!
//! Lib::Mem::fill(buffer, 0, length);
//! ```
//!
//! The `import _` lines below make the compiler read each file, which is what
//! adds its namespace to `Lib`. A file that no import reaches is not compiled,
//! even when assembly refers to its `@externName` symbols.

import _ from "./format";
import _ from "./mem";
import _ from "./scancode_queue";

/// Aggregate namespace of the library. The files above contribute
/// `Lib::Mem`, `Lib::Format` and `Lib::ScancodeQueue`.
export namespace Lib {}
